ay.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T14:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.959e5ee420c09268224304ec48876547438b9f60.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.959e5ee420c09268224304ec48876547438b9f60.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 12:05PM MDT until October 23 at 2:15PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding along the Conejos River and its tributaries is\nongoing in and around the communities of Conejos and Antonito due\nto excessive rainfall over the previous 48 hours.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 215 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of the Conejos River, area creeks, streams, and\nother low-lying and flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\nStreams continue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier\nrainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1202 PM MDT, Emergency management reported flooding in the\nwarned area. Stream gauges on the Conejos River and other\ntributaries, including the San Antonio River, are continuing to\nrise.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nManassa, Sanford, Antonito, Romeo, Conejos, Bountiful and Ortiz.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T14:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bc66efbf5c032093cfa229760fb132a1c7f4ae60.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bc66efbf5c032093cfa229760fb132a1c7f4ae60.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 7:40AM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Light to moderate rain showers will continue across the southwest\nmountains through the morning, with scattered showers and\npossible thunderstorms, developing across the region through the\nafternoon. Rain, locally heavy associated with the afternoon\nshowers and thunderstorms, will exacerbate ongoing flooding\nissues across the eastern San Juan mountains and Upper Rio Grande\nvalley.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T19:17:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 231917 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 117 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rain threat will develop over the eastern plains on Saturday into Sunday. - Some accumulation snow possible across the higher peaks Saturday afternoon and evening. - Mainly dry this upcoming week then another storm possible next weekend. && .SHORT TERM /THRO","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T17:58:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 231758 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1158 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-241800- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","ur